From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 08:56:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(kernel-views): pin cgroup controller parsing
 accumulation and whitespace

### What
Pins `parse_controllers`: OR-accumulation of cpu/memory/pids flags, empty-token skipping for trailing/double spaces, unknown-token rejection, and empty-input zero result.

### Why it matters
Controller parsing gates cgroup subtree delegation; replacing `|=` with `&=` drops previously parsed controllers on multi-token input, and deleting the empty-token arm turns benign whitespace into a permission error. No existing test exercises this function.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `|=` -> `&=` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `b"" => continue` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline: PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-kernel-views --lib parse_controllers_accumulates`.

Spec-Ref: cgroup v2 subtree_control documentation

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
index 461e7b7c..dcb29c11 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/cgroup.rs
@@ -466,4 +466,23 @@ mod tests {
         );
         cg.remove(b"/c.slice", 0).unwrap();
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn parse_controllers_accumulates_and_skips_empty_tokens() {
+        // single controller
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b"+cpu"), Ok(CPU));
+        // multiple controllers accumulate via OR
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b"+cpu +memory"), Ok(CPU | MEMORY));
+        assert_eq!(
+            parse_controllers(b"+cpu +memory +pids"),
+            Ok(CPU | MEMORY | PIDS)
+        );
+        // trailing/double spaces produce empty tokens that must be skipped, not error
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b"+cpu "), Ok(CPU));
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b"+cpu  +pids"), Ok(CPU | PIDS));
+        // unknown token rejected
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b"+io"), Err(ViewError::PermissionDenied));
+        // empty input yields zero controllers
+        assert_eq!(parse_controllers(b""), Ok(0));
+    }
 }
